      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
      }
