       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose. Higher doses don't improve glycemic control, but they do raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects. I can't think of a clinical situation where this dose would help the patient.\n\nYou still have options:\n- **Enter a different dose now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum), or a lower dose if you'd like to titrate up. I can enter either right away.\n- **Check with pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's a reason for an above-maximum dose, they can review it. If it's approved, it can be entered through their process with the rationale documented.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** This could be a typo for 850 mg or 1,700 mg/day total.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
